	spec: 'Hal has one concept, tools: READ, BASH, EDIT and the rest are tools, never actions, in code (native-tool.ts, call-text.ts, Tool.syntax/SyntaxSpec, ToolCallBlock.cmd, scripts/tool), docs, prompts and tasks. Providers see one native tool, tool { cmd: string }, described as "Call one tool. Make independent calls in parallel." with the call syntax and examples in the cmd description; SYSTEM.md has # Tools and # Other tools, and HELP, errors and the extras speak of tools and calls. That model-facing text is exactly the change benchmarked on claude-sonnet-5-5 (11/11 tasks, no tool-name errors, no different from Action); other model-facing wording changes need user approval. README.md (Tools) and tasks/README.md explain to humans, never to the model, why Hal uses one native tool taking a command string: compact descriptions, a fixed native tool list that keeps the prompt cache across tool changes, one concept, HELP on demand, terminal-like calls, lenient parsing by Hal instead of provider schema rejection, and one tool across providers. Invariant: histories written before the rename (native Action { action }, block field action) still display, replay and resume: historyCheck.check reads them as tool { cmd } and cmd, and replay sends every call as tool { cmd } text (an unresolved call as the text the model wrote), which providers accept against the current definition.',
